  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 956 PM CDT Sun Aug 16 2026\n\nAfter Wednesday, the upper-ridge will begin to flatten and shift\nback to the west over the southern Rockies and Great Basin. This\nwill place the Tennessee Valley into northwest flow aloft, opening\nus up to a couple of shortwaves that will push through the area\nThursday and Friday, resulting in medium (30-60%) chances for\nshowers and thunderstorms both afternoons. A front will sag south\nof the area by the weekend, keeping the better chances for showers\nand storms displaced to south of us across central and south \nAlabama. This will also give us a relative break from the heat as \nhighs will drop to the upper 80s to lower 90s, with overnight lows\nin the 60s by the weekend.",
